35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings suggest a cautionary tale. Tools requiring universal daily input tend to fail, while specialized, narrow tools persist. Furthermore, many cross-unit efforts collapsed due to a lack of ownership. We must prioritize sustainability over ambition.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that the capital budget is frozen, but there's some room in the software allowance. Also, per-head licenses get more expensive as we add departments, while fixed-fee work has stayed stable. I'm worried about the long-term costs.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Oh boy, I found some big problems! Half the customer plants have no signal for whole afternoons, and getting devices approved takes forever! Also, our developers are super busy until the third quarter. We have to be careful!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My research confirms significant operational waste. We are losing nearly two hours daily in the depot and planning office just copying existing records. Additionally, eleven misrouted deliveries occurred because different units hold conflicting addresses for the same firms.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings are concerning. The coordination group is understaffed, with two people still writing logs by hand. Furthermore, clerks are repeatedly requesting the same certificates from vendors. We are wasting human effort on redundant, manual tasks.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji @Asuka, your findings align perfectly. We have a clear pattern of redundant manual labor and data inconsistency. If we can solve these without requiring universal daily entry, we may find a sustainable path forward.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, I agree. But if we choose something that uses per-head licenses, the cost will keep growing as more people use it. Maybe a fixed-fee project would be safer since the capital budget is frozen?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that's a great point! But we also have to think about the developers! If we pick something that needs a lot of coding right now, we might be stuck since they're so busy. We need a plan that actually works!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, correct. We must avoid projects that rely on unavailable developers or unstable network environments. The priority should be a solution that addresses the data duplication and misrouting I discovered, provided it is operationally lean.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I agree. We must prioritize a solution that eliminates these manual redundancies without adding more burden to an already depleted staff. Any proposal that requires extensive new administrative oversight is simply not viable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,It seems we are all converging on a need for efficiency and stability. We must seek a solution that targets these redundancies but remains narrow enough to be maintained without overwhelming our staff or budget.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. If we can find a project that fits within the software allowance and doesn't rely on those expensive per-head licenses, it would be much safer for us in the long run.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm with you! We need something that doesn't need a super-strong signal at the plants and doesn't make our poor developers cry because they're already so busy! Let's find a project that's just right!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The evidence points toward a critical need for data synchronization. The misrouted deliveries and the time wasted copying records are concrete losses. We should look for a candidate that centralizes data to eliminate these specific redundancies.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I agree. Centralizing data would directly address the redundant certificate requests and the manual logging I found. We need a tool that automates the flow of information rather than adding more manual entry for the staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We have a clear consensus on the criteria: it must solve data redundancy, avoid universal daily entry, fit the software budget, and not depend on immediate developer availability or plant network stability. I look forward to the candidates.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I hope the candidates fit these rules. I'm still a bit worried about the budget, but if we're all careful, I think we can find something that works. I'll wait for the list.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'm ready too! I've got my checklist all set! No bad signals, no stressed-out developers, and no scary costs! I bet one of the ideas is going to be perfect! Let's see them!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. We have established a rational framework for evaluation. Now we simply need to see which candidate aligns with these operational realities and constraints. I am ready to review the proposals.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I concur. We have a rigorous set of constraints. I will be looking for a proposal that reduces the administrative burden on our current staff rather than increasing it. I am ready to see the candidates.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
